<title>AUSTRALIA: Mobil plans Australian asset sale - paper.</title>
<headline>Mobil plans Australian asset sale - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Corp's Australian unit is planning to sell nearly A$400 million of local assets inherited from its takeover of oil producer and explorer Ampolex Ltd last year, the Sydney Morning Herald newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>The paper said the assets were likely to be keenly sought by emerging petroleum producers.</p>
<p>It said most of the assets would be located in the highly prospective waters off the northwest coast of Australia.</p>
<p>Mobil Exploration and Producing Australia exploration manager Scott Mulcahy told the newspaper the asset review was continuing.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
